 "catalogCode": "25396U",
 "notes": [
  "The Geography major may be declared after completion of two lower-division requirements. Students are able to use community college coursework as substitutions for lower-division requirements with approval from the Undergraduate Major Advisor. Transfer students should meet with the Undergraduate Major Advisor prior to enrollment to avoid course duplication.\nTo declare, make an appointment with the Undergraduate Major Advisor.\nGeography Major Requirements\nStudents must complete 3 lower-division courses and 8 upper-division courses in order to satisfy the Geography major requirements.\nGeneral Guidelines:\n- Substitutions: A maximum of 2 lower-division courses and 2 upper-division courses from related fields may be applied to the major if they are approved by the Undergraduate Major Advisor. If a student studies abroad, a maximum of 3 courses from their program may be applied as substitutes to the major requirements if they are approved by the Undergraduate Major Advisor. GEOG 198 and/or GEOG 199 can be applied to any UD area, depending on the subject matter, if approved by the Undergraduate Major Advisor.\n- GPA Requirements: At least 2.0 in all courses for the major.\n- Emphasis: Students can earn an emphasis by completing a total of 4 courses in a specific research area."
